WEBVTT

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:15.700
Wh-What's going on here?

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.330
I-I don't know.

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:20.540
I've never seen an event like this.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.800
The city of Ted is on fire?!

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:01.010
Chance of Survival 0.1%

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:11.400
Run!

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.150
Hurry!

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:16.950
Wh-What?

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.240
What's wrong? What happened?

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:22.040
Shut up! Outta my way!

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.840
Excuse me! Could you tell me what--

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:30.960
Get out of my way!

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:36.010
Someone tell me what's happening!

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:39.390
This is what happens in a panic.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:44.230
Everyone's looking out for themselves. They
won't stop to explain everything to you.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.150
But this is a game!

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:50.820
Look. Let's ask the blacksmith
while he fixes your sword.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.820
Pardon me, but

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.410
my sword is rusted.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.240
Could you remove the rust?

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:02.080
Are you stupid?
This ain't no time for that!

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:06.960
Then could you just
explain what's going on?

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.880
Are you asking for real?

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.590
Well...

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.880
The damn goblins attacked!

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.630
The goblins?

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:19.510
But isn't this city surrounded by
a moat so the goblins can't get in?

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:21.850
Yes. It's supposed to be.

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:26.190
The biggest drought in
50 years dried up the moat!

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:29.400
So those things took
the opportunity to attack!

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:33.690
A goblin assault.
I never knew that could happen.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:37.740
So I'll finally get to fight a monster!

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:41.160
Um, could you remove the rust after all?

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:44.200
Weren't you listening? Ain't no time!

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:48.080
If you remove the rust,
I can fight the goblins!

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:51.630
Not my problem! It's your fault
for neglecting your blade!

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:55.260
But it was rusted when I got it!

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:58.590
It wasn't your sword? Where'd you find it?

00:03:58.590 --> 00:03:59.720
My room.

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:01.510
Are you screwing with me?!

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.010
Argh! I've wasted
enough time on this idiot!

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:07.730
There's a whetstone right there!
Do it yourself!

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:10.100
Um... how do I do it?

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:15.610
Scrape the whetstone from the
hilt to the tip of the sword! Idiot!

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:20.200
Scrape it with the whetstone?

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.910
L-Like this?

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:37.550
This rust is pretty tough.

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:38.550
Run!

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:39.470
This way!

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:41.760
Go, go!

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:42.640
Hurry!

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:43.510
They're here!

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.270
It's a goblin!

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:47.270
Help!

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:49.480
Please!

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:51.810
Screw it!

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.980
Wh-What's wrong, Hiro?

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:55.400
What <i>isn't </i>wrong?

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.070
What kind of RPG protagonist stands by

00:04:57.070 --> 00:05:00.900
just going scrape, scrape, scrape
while the town is attacked?

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:04.580
But you need to remove
the rust to use the sword.

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:06.700
It'll still do as a club!

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.290
St-St-Stop!

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:09.660
Absolutely not!

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.670
Goblins have ogre-like strength!

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:13.540
Even though they're smaller.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:15.540
R-Reona?

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.710
You have no chance of winning!

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:20.010
You're 120% sure to die!

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:22.680
B-But the townspeople!

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.350
Hiro, stay calm and listen.

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:27.890
I need to tell you something.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:33.900
If you die in Kiwame Quest,
something terrible will happen to you.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.520
C-Come to think of it...

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:40.440
I don't know what happens if I die!

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.820
D-Don't tell me...

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:44.160
If I die in the game...

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:48.160
...do I die in real life, too?

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.540
You read too much manga!

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:53.210
The game <i>does </i>pursue ultimate realism,

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:57.040
but that whole death game
thing is just ridiculous!

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.920
Th-Then what is it?

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:01.130
You break something.

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:02.800
Break something?

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.720
Like a part of my body?

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:09.850
No, what I mean is,
if you die while playing KQ...

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:14.060
Bam!

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:16.560
...both your console and your game break!

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.610
What?

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.730
Not just the game but the console, too?!

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:21.610
That's right!

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:23.400
What the hell?!

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:27.990
Seriously, how did that design
not become a huge problem?

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:32.000
Hiro, I'm sure you
already had an inkling, but

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.000
this is the ultimate shitty game.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:37.630
Reona...

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.920
you finally acknowledged it.

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:42.590
If the player dies, the console dies, too.

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:48.430
Over the past ten years, many users have
filed lawsuits over the death system.

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:53.890
"Suing a Game Company?"
"Techno Mosuke Inc."

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:51.430
Though the company apparently
used its massive power and wealth

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:54.560
to quash any problems.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:59.940
The outcry even extended to retail stores,
which were flooded with claims.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:03.190
Returned

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:03.650
Furthermore, various other
problems were manifest,

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:11.240
so soon after release, KQ was buried as a
next-level supremely shitty full-dive RPG.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:16.710
Now you get why you'd have to pay
someone to take it off your hands, right?

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:19.840
Then <i>why </i>did you
sell it to me at list price?

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:21.550
Anyway,

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:23.840
let's log out for now.

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:24.880
Huh?

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:30.010
It's not very good to rely on game guides,
but goblins are crazy strong.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.890
Let's take a look at
the Auberdine Walkthrough.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:34.060
Ahuh...

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:36.270
Now then, triple tap.

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:39.350
Save your adventure and quit the game?

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:42.730
Thank goodness.
It's still possible to save.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:44.230
Okay, let's bail.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.570
U-Um, just one peek!

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:50.490
Can I just take one
little peek at a goblin?

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:53.490
Fine. But just a quick look.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:55.450
Thanks!

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:10.010
I-It's so realistic!

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:11.970
You could think it's
a newly discovered animal!

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:14.600
Hey, not so loud!

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:18.600
Oh, man! I can't wait
to battle this thing!

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:26.990
Mommy!

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:29.700
Reona! A little girl!

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:32.160
W-Wait, Hiro!

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:35.740
You'll die if you fight it!

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:38.410
Is that what you want?
The console list price is 100,000 yen!

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:41.420
FYI, I sell it for 129,800 yen!

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.210
That's highway robbery!

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:46.460
If my console does break,
no way am I buying from you!

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:48.840
Anyway, let's approach this rationally!

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:54.720
The girl is only an NPC! She's just a
software simulation of human intellect!

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:58.350
Don't put it so coldly!

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:01.940
She looks just like a little girl!

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:04.150
Besides...

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:08.190
Never again.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:09.950
Just because it's an NPC,

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:13.410
I can't just let a person die
or be killed in front of me.

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:17.120
I don't want any more death.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.660
H-Hiro...

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:25.000
Are you...

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.300
a lolicon?

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:27.920
Seriously?! No!

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:30.590
Oh, look!

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:34.390
It's the Guard! The City Guard is here!

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:36.390
Damned monster!

00:09:36.390 --> 00:09:39.310
Stay back or we'll chop you up!

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:58.700
Y-You bastard!

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:07.960
Take th--

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.300
Wh-What the hell?!

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:20.720
Also, I just said no more death,
and two people immediately died!

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:24.520
Do you get how fearsome goblins are now?

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:27.940
<i>That's </i>the first monster you fight?

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:34.320
Nearly all players who managed to
leave Ted avoided fighting the goblins.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.620
O-Oh, I see.

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:40.330
But can I do that in this situation?

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:55.470
H-Have any players ever defeated a goblin?

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:59.430
To my knowledge, just two:
Kamui and SHOW HEY.

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:03.560
I know about Kamui,
but who's this SHOW HEY?

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:09.110
Shouhei Aida. In real life he became the
Oriental and Pacific Boxing Champion.

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:09.940
Say what?

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:14.280
When asked in an interview to name
the strongest boxer he'd ever faced,

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:16.200
"Definitely goblins"

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.610
was supposedly his answer!

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:20.030
Come on! Goblins aren't boxers!

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.240
A-Anyway, I'm gonna save them!

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:24.710
Are you serious? Do you wanna die?

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:27.170
I'll find a moment to help them escape!

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:29.790
I think that might be doable!

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:34.720
Man, Hiro. Where's all
this fire coming from?

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:40.680
Fine. If you do die and ruin your console,
I'll give you a discount--105,000 yen.

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:43.680
The discount price is
still above list price...

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:46.060
But <i>first</i>...

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:50.400
The blacksmith left those behind.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:52.190
Let's change those pants.

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:55.110
That old dude's pants?

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.650
Don't like the idea of that.

00:11:56.650 --> 00:12:00.320
Would you rather go out
there reeking of ammonia?

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:03.240
I-Isn't time of the essence?

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.160
Do it right now! Put them on!

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:09.080
I'm sick of the smell!
You've reeked this whole time!

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:22.470
Mommy! Help me!

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:34.070
I'm invisible, so I'll distract him.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:37.570
You use that time to save the girl.

00:12:37.570 --> 00:12:39.240
G-Got it.

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:42.410
We can at least save the girl.

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:44.450
There was nothing we could do.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:47.580
Don't dwell on it.

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:51.330
Maybe if we hadn't
stopped to change pants...

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:52.630
No! Focus!

00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:55.630
Focus on saving the girl!

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:57.670
Okay. Here I go!

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:07.810
Take this!

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:12.730
Now!

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:19.190
Come on!

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:23.160
All right! It worked!

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:31.870
Th-There were <i>two</i>?!

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:37.760
I-It's all over.

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:43.930
Who was I kidding?

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:46.010
Are you okay?

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:50.100
Kaede?

00:13:56.820 --> 00:13:57.690
Run!

00:13:57.690 --> 00:13:58.780
What?

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:00.900
Listen, you have to run!

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:06.700
I'm right here! Go after me!

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:13.170
Bastard!

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:36.060
C-Come on!

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:04.300
Wh-What just happened?

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:06.180
That was amazing, Hiro!

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:09.010
That was pro athlete-level dashing!

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:14.440
I-I'm not sure how I did it.
Though I've always been a fast runner.

00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:17.400
Was it the power of adrenaline?

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:19.400
But I'm in the game world.

00:15:19.400 --> 00:15:22.690
So was it a bug in the game?

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:33.000
Despite my display,
the situation hasn't changed at all.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.540
I guess this is it.

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:40.210
No, we're saved!

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:52.260
Tesla!

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:53.970
Hiro, are you all right?

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:56.600
Yeah, but...

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:03.860
Lightning Extreme!

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:15.080
I-Incredible!

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:19.790
Possessing superhuman agility due
to natural talent and intensive training,

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:21.790
he's the strongest Guardsman in Ted!

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:24.670
Tesla Wolff Carmine!

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:29.510
Also known as "Thundering Tesla," after
the lightning-like look of his gold armor.

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:32.970
He's the strongest NPC
you meet in the early game.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:34.350
You've done your homework.

00:16:34.350 --> 00:16:36.390
Because he's pretty.

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:40.650
The City Guard.

00:16:40.650 --> 00:16:43.820
Tesla, sir! Brilliantly done!

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:48.400
Escort this girl to her home.

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:51.910
The rest of you, start dealing
with the burning homes.

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:53.990
Yes, sir!

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:55.870
Let's get you home. dear.

00:16:55.870 --> 00:16:58.290
O-Okay.

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:06.510
I actually feel a little
like an RPG hero now.

00:17:08.050 --> 00:17:10.380
Hero, a new title!

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:15.350
It says, "Lolita Complex Best Friend
Killer: Amicide Who Likes Little Girls."

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:17.060
What the hell?!

00:17:17.060 --> 00:17:21.440
Now, now. Looking at it
objectively, even I thought so.

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:24.610
I thought, "I bet he
wants that girl to like him."

00:17:24.610 --> 00:17:27.230
What is <i>wrong </i>with you?!

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:31.110
Ugh, you totally ruined the moment.

00:17:34.120 --> 00:17:39.910
Oh, shit! NPCs can't see Reona.
He'll think I'm crazy!

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:44.080
Hiro, I see you're a warrior, too.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:45.460
E-Excuse me?

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:51.930
Perhaps it's an insensitive request,
but I need as many warriors as I can get.

00:17:51.930 --> 00:17:53.640
W-Warrior?

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:58.520
Hiro, you'd be well compensated.
It could even just be temporary.

00:17:58.520 --> 00:18:01.600
Would you join the
City Guard as a mercenary?

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:04.310
A mercenary? An RPG classic!

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:07.230
And I'd get to fight alongside Tesla?

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:09.650
I will! I'd be glad to join!

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:11.360
Thank you.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:14.240
H-Hey! Shouldn't you think about it more?

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:18.450
It'll be fine! Near Tesla
is the safest place to be.

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:21.000
Well, I suppose so...

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:23.870
Then come with me when you're ready, Hiro.

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:29.510
The City Guard training grounds are on
Queen Govern's estate. I'll guide you.

00:18:29.510 --> 00:18:30.960
Right. Yes.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:34.430
This feels like a save point
before a big event.

00:18:34.430 --> 00:18:37.100
This was enough for today, I think.

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:38.470
I'll stop here, Reona.

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:40.680
Oh, of course.

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:41.350
Save your adventure and quit the game?

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:43.020
Look at the walkthr--

00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:50.650
All right! It finally feels like a game!

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:59.280
Hey, are you still
playing that shitty game?

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:00.790
Yeah.

00:19:00.790 --> 00:19:02.500
How do you stand it?

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:05.210
Yeah, there's a lot to gripe about.

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:11.300
But get this. Supposedly, if you die,
the game breaks your console.

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:15.470
Wait, <i>what</i>?! I don't
even know where to begin.

00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:17.720
Can you believe that?

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:22.720
That's beyond the category
of shitty game. Like, hard pass.

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:24.730
No kidding.

00:19:26.730 --> 00:19:28.440
Hiro.

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:30.150
You seem happy.

00:19:30.150 --> 00:19:31.900
I-I do?

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:38.240
Well, they say you complain
most about things you love.

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:39.450
Love?

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:42.700
I love KQ?

00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:47.460
A ridiculous level of extreme difficulty.

00:19:47.460 --> 00:19:50.250
Game over means the end of your console.

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:54.090
That it's a shitty game
is an indisputable fact...

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:01.560
Guess I'll play some KQ when I get home.

00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:13.570
All set.

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:16.990
Maybe I should check first.

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:18.690
"AUBERDINE WALKTHROUGH"

00:20:16.990 --> 00:20:19.360
Hmm.

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:22.820
ABOUT THE GOBLIN ASSAULT

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.530
Ah, here it is.

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:29.170
Hey, trash. You've really done it now.

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:30.540
Huh?

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:34.210
There are many ways to leave Ted.

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:38.510
The typical route is to complete many
townspeople's requests, gain reputation,

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:41.930
and thereby obtain Queen
Govern's permission to leave.

00:20:41.930 --> 00:20:45.640
It's a hassle but it's the surest way.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.980
Or you could flee the city

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:51.900
and head for Flora Castle while
running from the goblins outside.

00:20:51.900 --> 00:20:57.190
This move is only available
to highly skilled martial artists.

00:20:57.190 --> 00:21:01.530
There are yet other methods,
but the worst is the goblin assault event.

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:04.200
The options for leaving
the city are limited.

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:08.000
I'll reveal them,
so be grateful, you dimwit!

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.540
Just as infuriating as always.

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:13.540
Option one: Fight with allies.

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:17.170
Recommended if you can
get 100 total NPC and PCs.

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:20.090
Though you'll never get
that many, you loner loser!

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:23.010
Chance of survival: five percent.

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:26.600
Option two: Hide from
the goblins for four days.

00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:29.690
You dig a hole under
some house and hide in it.

00:21:29.690 --> 00:21:32.150
But if you do, you'll never
be able to leave the city.

00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:34.230
Sucks to be you, mole bastard!

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:36.860
Chance of survival: ten percent.

00:21:36.860 --> 00:21:41.530
Option three: Join the City Guard
as a merc and fight alongside Telsa.

00:21:41.530 --> 00:21:43.030
Here we go.

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:46.240
Actually, this is the most awful option.

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:47.910
Wha--?

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:51.540
Even I, genius that I am,
find this option difficult.

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:55.590
For a fat, stupid, dimwitted,
garbage turd like you, it's impossible.

00:21:55.590 --> 00:21:58.630
Chance of survival: 0.1 percent.

00:21:58.630 --> 00:22:00.470
Die!

00:22:00.470 --> 00:22:03.680
What?!

00:22:03.680 --> 00:22:09.140
Zero point one percent
chance of survival means...

00:22:09.140 --> 00:22:14.610
...99.9% chance to ruin my console!

00:23:46.030 --> 00:23:49.410
Episode 8: Enlistment and Baptism.
